using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Data.SqlClient;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public static class ConnectionPoolHelper
{
    public static async Task<List<Task<SqlDataReader>>> ExecuteBatchAsync(List<string> sqlCommands, string connectionString, int maxConcurrentConnections)
    {
        var tasks = new List<Task<SqlDataReader>>();

        using (var connectionPool = new SqlConnectionPool(connectionString))
        {
            foreach (var sqlCommand in sqlCommands)
            {
                try
                {
                    var task = ExecuteAsync(sqlCommand, connectionPool);
                    tasks.Add(task);
                }
                catch (Exception ex)
                {
                    // Handle potential exceptions here
                }
            }
        }

        return await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
    }

    private static async Task<SqlDataReader> ExecuteAsync(string sqlCommand, SqlConnectionPool connectionPool)
    {
        using (var connection = await connectionPool.GetConnectionAsync())
        {
            var command = new SqlCommand(sqlCommand, connection);
            return await command.ExecuteReaderAsync();
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a `SqlConnectionPool` to manage database connections efficiently and ensures that the maximum number of concurrent connections is not exceeded. The `ExecuteBatchAsync` method accepts a list of SQL commands, a connection string, and a maximum number of concurrent connections as input. It creates a new `SqlConnectionPool` using the provided connection string and then iterates over the SQL commands in the list. For each command, it creates a new `Task<SqlDataReader>` that executes the command asynchronously using the `ExecuteAsync` method. The `ExecuteAsync` method uses the `GetConnectionAsync` method of the `SqlConnectionPool` to obtain a connection from the pool and then executes the SQL command using the `SqlCommand` class. Finally, the `ExecuteBatchAsync` method returns a list of all the tasks that were created for each SQL command in the input list.

It's important to note that this code assumes that the SQL commands are valid and do not contain any syntax errors or other issues that could cause the database connection to fail. It also assumes that the `SqlConnectionPool` is properly configured with the maximum number of concurrent connections allowed."]

