using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Xml;
using System.Xml.XPath;

public static List<string> ParseXml(string xml, string xpathQuery, int maxSize)
{
    if (xml == null)
        throw new ArgumentNullException("xml");

    var navigator = new XPathNavigator(new XmlDocument().CreateNavigator());
    try
    {
        navigator.PushNode(xml);
    }
    catch (XmlException ex)
    {
        throw new Exception("Failed to parse XML document", ex);
    }

    var elements = new List<string>();
    foreach (XPathNavigator nav in navigator.Select(xpathQuery))
    {
        if (elements.Count >= maxSize)
        {
            LogWarning("Truncating list of elements");
            break;
        }

        elements.Add(nav.Value);
    }

    return elements;
}
```
This function takes in an XML document, an XPath query string, and a maximum size for the returned list as input. It uses the `XPathNavigator` class to navigate the XML document and select nodes that match the specified XPath query. The function then iterates over the selected nodes and adds their values to a list of strings.

The function first checks if the provided XML document is null, and throws an exception if it is. It then creates a new `XmlDocument` object and uses its `CreateNavigator()` method to create an `XPathNavigator` object that can be used to navigate the XML document. The function then pushes the root node of the XML document onto the navigator's stack, which allows it to begin navigating the document.

The function then uses the `Select()` method of the `XPathNavigator` class to select nodes in the XML document that match the specified XPath query. The function iterates over these selected nodes and adds their values to a list of strings. If the maximum size for the returned list is exceeded, the function logs a warning message indicating that elements have been truncated and breaks out of the loop.

The function finally returns the list of strings containing the values of the selected XML elements. If the provided XML document is null or if the XPath query fails to execute, the function throws an exception.']

