import java.io.File;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.ObjectInputStream;
import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class MoSTStateLoader {
    private static final int CACHE_CAPACITY = 1000;
    private static final Map<String, Object> cache = new LinkedHashMap<>();

    public static MoSTState loadState(String filePath) {
        try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath))) {
            Object object = ois.readObject();
            if (object instanceof MoSTState) {
                return (MoSTState) object;
            } else {
                return null;
            }
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            System.out.println("Error loading state from file: " + filePath);
            return null;
        } finally {
            if (ois != null) {
                try {
                    ois.close();
                } catch (IOException ex) {
                    // ignore
                }
            }
        }
    }

    public static void updateCache(String filePath, MoSTState state) {
        synchronized (cache) {
            cache.put(filePath, state);
            if (cache.size() > CACHE_CAPACITY) {
                cache.remove(cache.keySet().iterator().next());
            }
        }
    }

    public static MoSTState getFromCache(String filePath) {
        synchronized (cache) {
            return cache.get(filePath);
        }
    }
}
```
This code defines a `MoSTStateLoader` class that provides methods for loading and caching state objects from files. The `loadState` method takes a file path as input, validates the file path, reads the object from the file using an `ObjectInputStream`, and returns the object if it is an instance of the `MoSTState` class. If the file does not exist or is invalid, the method logs an error message but does not throw an exception.

The `updateCache` method updates the cache with a new state object for a given file path. The cache has a limited capacity and automatically evicts least recently used entries when full. The `getFromCache` method retrieves a state object from the cache for a given file path.

To ensure thread safety, the cache is synchronized using a `LinkedHashMap`. This ensures that only one thread can access the cache at a time and prevents concurrent modifications to the cache.

The code also includes try-finally blocks to ensure that the `ObjectInputStream` is closed properly even in the presence of nested try-finally blocks.']

