$client = new \League\OAuth2\Client\Provider\GenericProvider([
    'clientId' => getenv('CLIENT_ID'),
    'clientSecret' => getenv('CLIENT_SECRET'),
    'redirectUri' => getenv('REDIRECT_URI'),
    'urlAuthorize' => getenv('URL_AUTHORIZE'),
    'urlAccessToken' => getenv('URL_ACCESS_TOKEN'),
]);

// Handle user authentication flow
if (isset($_GET['code'])) {
    // Exchange authorization code for access token
    $accessToken = $client->getAccessToken($_GET['code']);

    // Store access token in session storage
    $_SESSION['access_token'] = $accessToken;
} elseif (isset($_SESSION['access_token'])) {
    // Use existing access token from session storage
    $accessToken = $_SESSION['access_token'];
} else {
    // Redirect user to authorization URL
    header('Location: ' . $client->getAuthorizationUrl());
    exit();
}

// Cache access token for improved performance during repeated API calls
$cache = new \Doctrine\Common\Cache\FilesystemCache(__DIR__ . '/cache');
if ($cache->contains('access_token')) {
    $accessToken = $cache->fetch('access_token');
} else {
    $cache->save('access_token', $accessToken);
}

// Use access token to make API calls
$apiClient = new \GuzzleHttp\Client([
    'base_uri' => getenv('API_BASE_URI'),
    'headers' => [
        'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $accessToken,
    ],
]);

// Handle API response
$response = $apiClient->get('/users');
if ($response->getStatusCode() === 200) {
    // Process API response
} else {
    // Handle error response
}
```
This script uses the `Dotenv` library to load environment variables from a `.env` file, and the `League\OAuth2\Client` library for handling OAuth2 authentication. The script also uses the `Doctrine\Common\Cache\FilesystemCache` class for caching access tokens, which improves performance during repeated API calls.

The script first loads the vendor autoloader to include the necessary classes for the OAuth2 client and caching mechanism. It then initializes an instance of the `GenericProvider` class from the `League\OAuth2\Client` library, which is used to handle the user authentication flow. The script checks if an authorization code was provided in the URL query parameters, and if so, it exchanges it for an access token using the `getAccessToken()` method of the `GenericProvider` instance.

If no authorization code is provided, the script redirects the user to the authorization URL using the `getAuthorizationUrl()` method of the `GenericProvider` instance. The script then stores the access token in session storage using the `$_SESSION` superglobal.

The script also uses the `Doctrine\Common\Cache\FilesystemCache` class to cache the access token for improved performance during repeated API calls. If a cached access token is found, it is used instead of making a new API call. The script then creates an instance of the `GuzzleHttp\Client` class using the `base_uri` and `headers` options set to the API base URI and the authorization header with the access token, respectively.

The script then makes a GET request to the `/users` endpoint of the API using the `get()` method of the `GuzzleHttp\Client` instance. If the response status code is 200 (OK), the script processes the API response. Otherwise, it handles the error response."]

