The code first determines the bits per sample and samples per pixel by reading the "BitsPerSample" and "SamplesPerPixel" tags in the TIFF file. It then handles cases where the image has extra samples by allocating memory for an array of structures containing information about each extra sample. If the bits per sample is not supported, it returns an appropriate error message.

