The function allocates memory for the key and IV using `malloc`, and ensures that all resources are properly cleaned up when the cipher is no longer needed by returning a pointer to the cipher context and implementing a function to handle cleanup, disabling the cipher, and freeing all associated resources.

The function handles errors gracefully and provides meaningful error messages if allocation fails or if the cipher setup is not successful."]

