This code block implements a C function that integrates cryptographic operations using the OpenSSL library and DNS resolution capabilities, leveraging an existing network stack library for seamless integration. The function accepts a string parameter representing a hostname and a command line option specifying the desired operation—either cryptographic transformation or DNS resolution. If the operation is cryptographic, it should utilize the OpenSSL library to perform the specified action and return a pointer to a cipher object. If the operation is DNS resolution, the function should resolve the given hostname to its corresponding IP address, supporting IPv6 addresses, and handle up to 10 simultaneous resolution requests with a timeout mechanism for each.

