The function uses a helper class `RandomValueHelper` to generate random values within a specified range for the `CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG`. The helper class has a private field for the minimum value, a private field for the maximum value, and methods for returning a random float value and a random integer value within the specified range.

The function synchronizes access to the list and the helper class using a mutex to prevent race conditions and ensure data integrity under concurrent modifications. It also validates that `RNTI` values fall within the valid range for the system and handles any invalid inputs gracefully.']

