To address the performance constraints, this code uses fixed-size buffers for the RRC messages, which reduces cache misses and improves data locality. It also employs techniques such as slab allocation or custom memory pools to manage memory more efficiently, reducing the overhead of memory allocation and deallocation in a performance-critical context.

To ensure memory safety and efficient resource management, this code limits the memory usage by implementing a mechanism that limits the application's consumption of excessive resources even under heavy load. It also considers memory fragmentation and its impact on performance, using techniques such as defragmentation or custom memory pools to manage memory more efficiently.

